How the rule maps onto the strategy:
- **Session return:** S(d) is the close of the 19:00 UTC bar divided by the open of the 13:00 UTC bar of the same UTC day, minus 1. If either of those two bars is missing, there is no signal that day.
- **Entry:** on the close of the 19:00 bar, Monday to Friday, when S(d) < 0.003 and volume is above zero. It fills at the 20:00 open.
- **Exit:** on the close of every 12:00 UTC bar that has volume, so the sell happens at the 13:00 open.
- **Backstop:** `custom_exit` closes any trade that has been open 17 hours or more, which covers missing or zero-volume bars.
- **Stop and settings:** `stoploss = -0.03`, `startup_candle_count = 24`, timeframe `"1h"`, no cooldown and no informative timeframe.

The test checks the class constants, that signals are binary, the entry and exit hours, the strict 0.003 threshold, no signal when the 13:00 bar is missing, no signal on zero volume or undefined start-up values, that appending future candles changes nothing, and the 17-hour backstop.

I didn''t change any rule. One of my own threshold tests failed at first because 100.3/100 − 1 comes out just under 0.003 in floating point, so I changed the test input to 100.31. One deprecation warning remains in my test file (`dt.dayofweek`). It doesn''t affect the result.','2026-11-06T23:12:07.418684+00:00');

