- **`S20261106T234421Z-2.json`, intraday jump continuation.** Buy after a 15m bar rises at least 4 times its recent volatility, only when the daily trend is up, and sell at the UTC day close. Estimate: 160 trades a year. The weak point: the paper (Saef et al.) only shows that a jump and that day''s return point the same way. It does not test a tradable rule, and the file says so. This one is fairly close to H-035.
- **`S20261106T234421Z-3.json`, breakout gated by a trend test.** Buy a break of the 24-hour high only when a variance-ratio test (variance of 1-hour returns vs. four times the variance of 15m returns) shows recent 15m returns are trending, with a 4-hour trend filter. Exit on a break of the 4-hour low or after 24 hours. Estimate: 170 trades a year. The main paper (Zargar & Kumar) is cited from its abstract only, which does not say whether the pattern it found is trending or reverting. It has the most free parameters of the three (6).

